2. Core abstractions

2.1 Field module

Interface (per field kind):

Identity:

field_id: UUID

field_kind: string

version: string

State:

state: opaque (binary/JSON; kernel never inspects)

Methods:

init(config) -> state

step(state, context) -> state

apply_patch(state, patch) -> state

validate(state, context) -> Violation[]

project(state, view_config) -> Geometry/Metadata

Fields: optics, structure, cost, thermal, permissions, etc.

2.2 Rule module

apply(fields, context) -> PatchSet

PatchSet = Patch[]

Patch = { field_id, patch_payload }

Rules implement evolution logic (physics, control, AI agents).

2.3 Constraint module

check(fields, context) -> Violation[]

Violation = { id, severity, scope, field_ids, code, message, metadata }

Constraints enforce physical, logical, economic, safety limits.

2.4 Global arbitration layer

Input: violations: Violation[], staged_state, context, policy_profile

Output: ResolutionPlan = { decision, actions[] }

ResolutionAction types:

ROLLBACK, REPAIR_PATCH, DEGRADE_MODE, CLAMP_INPUT, SKIP_RULE, QUARANTINE_SEGMENT

Uses declarative policies (YAML/JSON) to map violation patterns → actions.

2.5 Context

context.telemetry — latest normalized external data.

context.mode — NORMAL | SAFE | DEGRADED | DIAGNOSTIC.

context.policy_profile — active policy set.

context.metadata — run/session info.

3. Kernel lifecycle

Per tick:

Ingest

WebSocket → JSON → context.telemetry (validated, normalized).

Rule phase

For each rule:

patches += rule.apply(field_registry, context)

Staging

For each patch:

new_state = field.apply_patch(old_state, patch)

Build staged_fields.

Constraint phase

For each constraint:

violations += constraint.check(staged_fields, context)

Arbitration

plan = arbitrator.plan(violations, staged_fields, context, policy_profile)

Apply plan.actions (may mutate staged_fields, context, mode).

Optional single re‑check of constraints.

Decision

If plan.decision = COMMIT_WITH_FIXES → commit staged_fields.

If RETRY_TICK → bounded retry.

If ABORT_TICK → no commit; log + alert.

Projection

scene = projector.build_scene(fields)

Export:

3D assets: OBJ/MTL, GLTF/GLB

Metadata: telemetry snapshot, policy profile, cost, mode, hashes.

Transition logging

Compute hashes and signatures (below).

